            {
                "entry_id": "be24af87-9174-38ca-85c2-f38bb0973483",
                "word": "yin",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f55c0a81-1757-3e78-aca9-b138a58c92e9",
                        "entry_id": "be24af87-9174-38ca-85c2-f38bb0973483",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A principle in Chinese and related East Asian philosophies associated with dark, cool, female, etc. elements of the natural world."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "11e08dd3-b4af-4d04-92d6-993fc8cbc02e",
                                "sense_id": "f55c0a81-1757-3e78-aca9-b138a58c92e9",
                                "text": "\"Steamed fish and chicken and vegetable soup and even mushrooms are considered cooling foods, edible materializations of the yang, the pure primal air. The yin, or earth element, inheres in fried dishes and especially in shark's fin soup. Am I right, Mr Lee?\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "929a3c18-af61-4850-994e-b8385dcabec5",
                                "sense_id": "f55c0a81-1757-3e78-aca9-b138a58c92e9",
                                "text": "According to traditional Chinese medicine, blood carries chi, your “life force,” which fuels all the functions of the body. When you lose blood, you lose chi, and this causes your body to go into a state of yin (cold). When yin (cold) and yang (hot) are out of balance, your body will suffer physical disorders."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "214c589f-125b-4b76-8cb1-4274e8e1690c",
                                "sense_id": "f55c0a81-1757-3e78-aca9-b138a58c92e9",
                                "text": "In ancient Chinese philosophy, the opposing forces of Yin (passive, feminine, night) and Yang (active, masculine, sun) balance life.[…]\nAs we turn towards darker days (from November 1st until the winter solstice's darkest night on December 21st), we have a chance to turn inward for reflection. We enter a Yin phase."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eab4cbde-be0f-4f44-8138-fff4a7e2d1a3",
                        "source_entry_id": "be24af87-9174-38ca-85c2-f38bb0973483",
                        "source_sense_id": "f55c0a81-1757-3e78-aca9-b138a58c92e9",
                        "source_sense_description": "essential female principle",
                        "target_lang_word": "Yin",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Yin",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be9dd141-2879-398d-8e07-d8de7d4c2658",
                                        "entry_id": "f701c11c-6642-3306-9ad4-4f7ec28e6c23",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "das weibliche Prinzip in der chinesischen Naturphilosophie"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71642be2-3e2d-46c2-ab76-5c9dc17c460a",
                                                "sense_id": "be9dd141-2879-398d-8e07-d8de7d4c2658",
                                                "text": "Soviel weiß ich allerdings: das Yin-Yang-Symbol genießt in Ostasien die höchste Verehrung."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78367c97-2aba-4b08-94c8-5ce202992781",
                                                "sense_id": "be9dd141-2879-398d-8e07-d8de7d4c2658",
                                                "text": "„Ich glaube daran, dass wir Yin und Yang unserer Partei zusammenbringen müssen“, erläutert der Rechtsanwalt Mark Aronchick, einer der Gründer von VoteBoth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "621b672f-cfa2-41c6-a1b9-97cd07503aca",
                                                "sense_id": "be9dd141-2879-398d-8e07-d8de7d4c2658",
                                                "text": "Dieser Gott war ein Vegetations-, beileibe aber kein Schöpfergott, die Schöpfung wurde vielmehr durch das bipolare Spiel zwischen zwei Urkräften, dem männlichen Yang und dem weiblichen Yin bestimmt. In diesem Bild repräsentiert der Himmel das Prinzip Yang, die Erde folglich Yin, wobei sich alle Momente des Kosmos in Bewegung befinden und ein gewaltiges Durcheinander entstehen kann, welches die Dinge »unter dem Himmel« in ihrem Fortbestand bedroht."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4447300-5e26-409c-b01c-824342edbf10",
                                                "sense_id": "be9dd141-2879-398d-8e07-d8de7d4c2658",
                                                "text": "Bei Dusch-Gel und Bade-Öl erleben wir überhaupt Harmonie, Yin und Yang."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
